{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/agents/build-n-test.md .agents/skills/code-review-pr/references/review_checklist.md deps.edn'","aggregated_output":"---\ndescription: Build, lint, test commands, TDD guidelines, and bracket debugging for Clojure, ClojureScript, Node.js, and ClojureDart\n---\n\n# BUILD & TEST\n\n## Commands\n\n```sh\n# Tests (Babashka runner)\nbb test              # Run all tests (JVM, Node/CLJS, Dart/CLJD)\nbb test:clj          # JVM tests only (or: clj -M:test)\nbb test:cljs         # ClojureScript / Node tests (via shadow-cljs :cljs alias)\nbb test:cljd         # ClojureDart tests (requires flutter on PATH)\nnpm test             # Node.js tests\n\n# ClojureScript / shadow-cljs (always via deps.edn :cljs alias, never npx)\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch <build-id>    # e.g. watch demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build-id>  # e.g. compile demo\nclj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release <build-id>  # production release\n\n# ClojureDart\nclj -M:cljd compile\n\n# Linting\nclj -M:kondo --lint <path>\n```\n\n## Testing Philosophy & TDD\n\nWrite tests before implementing features (TDD).\n\nTests define the contract and expected behavior. Implementation follows from the tests, not the other way around.\n\nWhen implementing a feature or fix:\n1. **Red phase**: Write the test first — define what should happen.\n2. **Green phase**: Implement the minimum code to pass the test.\n3. **Refactor phase**: Refactor if needed while keeping tests green.\n\nThis ensures code is testable by design and implementation matches actual requirements.\n\n## Debugging Malformed CLJ / EDN / CLJS\n\nA single missing bracket can silently break an entire file. The compiler may still succeed, with subsequent forms nesting inside the broken one.\n\n1. **Run clj-kondo first**:\n   ```sh\n   clj -M:kondo --lint path/to/file.cljs\n   ```\n\n2. **If clj-kondo reports a mismatch, write a bracket-tracing script**:\n   Do NOT try to eyeball-count brackets. Track a stack of `(char, line, col)` for every opener. Handle: string literals, escaped chars, and `;;` line comments.\n\n3. **Fix one bracket at a time, re-run checker after each fix**:\n   Common patterns:\n   - Hiccup vector missing `]` causes siblings to become extra arguments.\n   - `defn`/`let` missing `)` causes subsequent top-level forms to nest inside.\n   - Both can coexist while total bracket count is zero-sum.\n\n4. **After brackets balance**, rerun `clj-kondo`, then rebuild with `clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile <build>`.\n# Code Review PR Checklist & Taxonomy\n\nWhen performing code reviews, evaluate changes using this structured checklist and severity taxonomy.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Finding Severity Taxonomy\n\n| Severity | Label | Definition | Examples |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **P0** | **Critical (Blocker)** | Security vulnerabilities, data loss risks, production crashes, secret leakage. Must be fixed before merging. | Hardcoded tokens, unhandled NullPointer on critical path, SQL injection, broken auth check. |\n| **P1** | **High (Must Address)** | Logic bugs, breaking API changes, missing error handling on external calls, race conditions, lack of tests for complex logic. | Swallowed exceptions, broken retry loop, missing backward compatibility in API schema. |\n| **P2** | **Medium (Recommended)** | Performance inefficiencies, code duplication, sub-optimal data structures, non-idiomatic style. | Unnecessary DB query inside loop, missing index, missing parameter validation. |\n| **P3** | **Low (Nit / Suggestion)** | Minor formatting, naming improvements, leftover comments/TODOs, minor doc polish. | Variable naming clarity, typos in docstrings, cleaning leftover TODO comments. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Comprehensive Review Checklist\n\n### A. Logic & Correctness\n- [ ] **Edge Cases**: Does the code handle null/nil/undefined, empty collections, zero values, boundary numbers, and unexpected inputs?\n- [ ] **State & Concurrency**: Are shared state mutations thread-safe? Are locks acquired/released properly without deadlock risks?\n- [ ] **Control Flow**: Are all conditional branches covered? Do loops have guaranteed termination conditions?\n- [ ] **Error Propagation**: Are errors caught and logged/surfaced appropriately, rather than swallowed silently (`catch (Exception e) {}`)?\n\n### B. Security & Credentials\n- [ ] **No Hardcoded Secrets**: Are API keys, passwords, bearer tokens, or private keys excluded from code and config?\n- [ ] **Input Validation & Sanitization**: Are external inputs validated before processing or passing to system shells, DB queries, or HTML rendering?\n- [ ] **Authentication & Authorization**: Do endpoints verify user identity and check permissions before executing state changes?\n- [ ] **Safe Dependencies**: Are newly added packages pinned to trusted versions without known vulnerabilities?\n\n### C. Architecture & API Design\n- [ ] **Preserve API Contracts**: Are public method signatures, REST endpoints, and schema definitions backward compatible?\n- [ ] **Single Responsibility**: Are modules, classes, and functions focused on a clear, single responsibility?\n- [ ] **Coupling & Cohesion**: Is the new code properly modularized without introducing circular dependencies or leaky abstractions?\n- [ ] **Idempotence**: Are retry loops or state-changing operations safe to re-execute on transient failures?\n\n### D. Performance & Resource Efficiency\n- [ ] **N+1 Queries**: Are database or remote API calls executed in batches rather than inside loops?\n- [ ] **Resource Cleanup**: Are file handles, database connections, streams, and web sockets closed explicitly (or managed via try-with-resources / context managers)?\n- [ ] **Memory & Allocation**: Are large datasets streamed or paginated rather than loaded fully into memory at once?\n\n### E. Test Coverage & Quality\n- [ ] **Test Coverage**: Do new features or bug fixes include corresponding unit or integration tests?\n- [ ] **Test Quality**: Do tests verify actual assertions rather than just checking that code runs without throwing?\n- [ ] **Edge Case Tests**: Are failure modes, invalid inputs, and error handlers covered by unit tests?\n\n---\n\n## 3. Review Feedback Guidelines\n\n1. **Be Specific**: Always reference the exact file line number, function name, and context.\n2. **Explain the \"Why\"**: Don't just say \"change this\". Explain the risk or benefit (e.g., \"This could lead to a race condition if two threads call `transact!` simultaneously...\").\n3. **Provide Concrete Fixes**: Offer concrete, copy-pasteable diff snippets where appropriate.\n4. **Acknowledge Good Work**: Highlight well-crafted solutions, thorough tests, or clean refactorings.\n{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n :cljd/opts {}\n :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"]\n :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}}\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\n           :dev {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}\n                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\n                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\n                              ;; generator only; production uses\n                              ;; dao.data.btree\n                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n                              {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n                 :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]}\n           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                  :extra-deps {tensegritics/clojuredart\n                               {:git/url \"https://github.com/tensegritics/ClojureDart.git\"\n                                :sha \"81b5c03a55cf52b21dc0be8ccfa4827b9889f488\"}}\n                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}}\n                    :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]\n                    :main-opts [\"-m\" \"world.server\"]}\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl\"]}\n           :cljs-yin-repl\n           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\" \"run\" \"yin.repl/-main\"]}\n           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl\"]}\n           :cljs-yin-repl\n           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\" \"run\" \"yin.repl/-main\"]}\n           :fmt {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :exec-fn tasks/fix-all}\n           :kondo {:extra-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version \"2026.01.19\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"clj-kondo.main\"]}\n           :telemetry-server {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.vm.telemetry-server.jvm\"]}\n           :dbg {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                 :main-opts [\"-m\" \"debug-cljd\"]\n                 :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :cljd-yin-repl\n           {:extra-deps {tensegritics/clojuredart\n                         {:git/url \"https://github.com/tensegritics/ClojureDart.git\"\n                          :sha \"81b5c03a55cf52b21dc0be8ccfa4827b9889f488\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.runner\"]}\n           :cljd-yin-repl-build\n           {:extra-deps {tensegritics/clojuredart\n                         {:git/url \"https://github.com/tensegritics/