y K holds the caller's return frame\\\"\\n   420\\t    (let [vm (run-segment\\n   421\\t               (assemble (segment 8)\\n   422\\t                         (instruction 0 :closure :yin.code/params '[x]\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_22\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-13 18:17:22 GMT\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-14 01:17:22 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\\n\\n**Verdict: request changes.** Two unresolved architecture defects prevent sign-off.\\n\\n| Severity | file:line | Invariant/evidence | Recommended correction |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| P1 | [semantic.cljc:600](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:600) | **Stable segment identity.** Loading silently replaces an existing segment image while retaining continuations that reference it. Reproduced: park in A, load different code B with A’s id, then resume A; execution returns B’s `:wrong-segment` instead of `:expected`. | Reject conflicting reuse of a segment id; allow identical reloads. Ensure batch tempids receive distinct identities before storage. Add a collision regression test. |\\n| P1 | [semantic.cljc:172](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:172) | **Pure-data continuations; no callbacks.** Passing `:restore-fn` into effect handling causes the shared engine to attach a host stream handle and a `:resume` closure to blocked wait entries via `runtime-adapter/vm-task`. Reproduced on empty `:stream-next`: `:resume` is a function and EDN round-trip fails. This is runtime-generated state, beyond §1.1’s allowance for program-supplied host values. | Keep wait/ready entries as data containing registers and resource ids. Resolve handles during polling and dispatch restoration explicitly. Preserve terminal-outcome checks and cursor updates; test serialization of blocked entries. |\\n\\nProperties that passed:\\n\\n- **Explicit control flow:** integer dispatch inside `loop/recur`; VM closure calls and returns do not recurse through host stacks.\\n- **§4 core transitions:** accumulator, environment, branch, call, return, store, and continuation operations follow the equations.\\n- **Tail-call bounds:** arguments/operator are removed and `K` is reused. The 100,000-call countdown reaches park with one caller frame and empty `St`.\\n- **Explicit `:vm/park`:** returns control without blocking a host thread, saving `{segment, pc+1, env, stack, k}` as data. Serialization and cross-segment resume pass when ids remain distinct.\\n- **No hidden global state:** interpreter registers and counters are explicit; dependencies are supplied at construction.\\n\\nValidation: **14 tests, 85 assertions passed under Babashka**, plus the two defect probes above. JVM, CLJS, and CLJD suites were not run. No files were modified.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"turn.completed\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":585290,\"cached_input_tokens\":529024,\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens\":3226,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":408}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
