{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '370,397p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md; sed -n '414,449p' test/yin/vm/semantic_test.cljc; rg -n 'cursor|defn run-once' src/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc test/yin/vm/test_utils.cljc; rg --files test/yin/vm | head -35\"","aggregated_output":"file the roadmap requires).\n\n### 3.5 Scheduler, park, resume\n\nThe VM record carries the engine's scheduler fields (`:ready-queue`,\n`:wait-set`, `:parked`, `:id-counter`, `:store`, `:blocked?`, `:halted?`)\nwith the same meanings. Wait entries built by the semantic `park-entry-fns`\nare `{:segment :pc :env :stack :k :reason :cursor-ref/:stream-id}` — pure\ndata: no resolved stream handle and no resume closure is ever attached to a\nwait or ready entry, so the wait set of a blocked machine survives an EDN\nround-trip (§1.1's serialization limit; the program's own `env`/stack values\naside). `engine/check-wait-set` resolves handles from the store on every\npoll, and restoration is dispatched explicitly. The restore function is\n\n```\nsemantic-restore : base entry val → base with control {:segment :pc},\n                                       env, stack, k, val from entry\n```\n\nand is handed to `engine/resume-from-run-queue` and\n`engine/resume-continuation`, exactly as `ast-walker-restore` is;\n`engine/resume-from-run-queue` runs the terminal-outcome check (a woken\nretry that ended `closed`/`cursor-mismatch`/… fails as the immediate\noperation would) before restoring. No `:restore-fn` is passed into\n`engine/handle-effect` or `engine/check-wait-set` from this evaluator, so\nnothing live rides on an entry. `engine/run-loop` drives `run`.\n\n### 3.6 Observation and traces\n(deftest segment-id-is-stable-test\n  (let [a (assemble (segment 4)\n                    (instruction 0 :const :yin.code/value :expected)\n                    (instruction 1 :push)\n                    (instruction 2 :park)\n                    (instruction 3 :halt))\n        ;; A different batch that reuses A's segment entity id — two batches\n        ;; minted independently, colliding on the id continuations name.\n        b (assemble (segment 3)\n                    (instruction 0 :const :yin.code/value :wrong-segment)\n                    (instruction 1 :park)\n                    (instruction 2 :halt))\n        vm (run-segment a)]\n    (testing \"A different image under the live id is rejected\"\n      (is (thrown-with-msg?\n            #?(:clj Exception :cljs js/Error :cljd Object)\n            #\"already holds different code\"\n            (semantic/vm-load-program vm b))))\n    (testing \"The rejected load leaves the image and parked continuation intact\"\n      (is (= seg (:segment (vm/value vm))))\n      (is (= 1 (count (:parked vm))))\n      (is (= :resumed (vm/value (run-segment vm (resume-segment :parked-0 :resumed))))\n          \"the parked continuation still resumes into A's code, not B's\"))\n    (testing \"An identical reload is accepted and keeps the parked continuation\"\n      (let [vm' (-> vm (semantic/vm-load-program a) vm/run)]\n        (is (= (:code vm) (:code vm')))\n        (is (= 2 (count (:parked vm')))\n            \"the reload ran to its own park without touching the first\")\n        (is (= :parked-1 (:id (vm/value vm'))))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Current continuation\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest current-continuation-test\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:14:     for a woken reader `:cursor`. Wait entries additionally carry `:reason`\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:15:     (`:next` or `:put`), `:stream` (a live v2 handle), and either `:cursor`\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:17:     hands it the handle and cursor it will be polled with. Cursors are\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:27:     :status :dao.stream/gap :cursor recovery}`, the terminal outcomes under\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:115:                            :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result)}]\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:118:    ;; A gap advances to the transport's recovery cursor. The reader is told\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:123:                             :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor result)}]\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:124:    (:dao.stream/cursor-mismatch :dao.stream/invalid-cursor\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:175:                          (stream/next (:stream entry) (:cursor entry)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:194:   Returns {:state updated-rt :result result-tag :value v :cursor c}.\"\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:195:  [rt handle cursor task]\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:196:  (let [result (stream/next handle cursor)\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:204:                                      :cursor cursor))\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:211:       :cursor (:cursor updates)})))\nsrc/cljc/dao/runtime.cljc:247:(defn run-once\ntest/yin/vm/code_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/semantic_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/ffi_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/engine_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/parity_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/module_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/test_utils.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/runtime_adapter_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/linearize_test.cljc\ntest/yin/vm/ast_walker_test.cljc\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
