{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-09-13 18:37:48 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-14 01:37:48 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\n\n**Sign-off: approved. Both previous P1 architecture defects are resolved.** No remaining defects found in the reviewed scope.\n\n| Severity | file:line | Invariant/evidence | Recommended correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Resolved P1 | [semantic.cljc:599](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:599) | Stable segment identity: `store-image`, invoked by `vm-load-program`, rejects conflicting images and accepts identical reloads. Regression tests verify parked continuations remain intact. | None. |\n| Resolved P1 | [engine.cljc:430](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:430) | Pure-data continuations: blocked entries retain resource IDs without injected handles or resume closures. Polling resolves handles; explicit restoration preserves terminal-error checks. Reader and writer entries pass EDN round-trip and wake-up tests. | None. |\n\nThe fixes preserve explicit control flow, immutable code images, and separation of loading from execution.\n\nValidation: **76 tests, 329 assertions passed under Babashka**, covering the semantic VM and shared engine, runtime adapter, FFI, and AST walker. JVM testing was blocked by sandbox cache-write restrictions; CLJS/CLJD were not run. No files were modified."}}
